f:[['Name','Meaning uncertain'],['Era','About 1500-1400 BC'],['Family','Brother of Moses and Miriam; wife Elisheba; sons Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar and Ithamar'],['Role','First high priest of Israel'],['Age','123; died on Mount Hor (Numbers 33:39)'],['Main passages','Exodus 4:14-16; 28-29; 32; Leviticus 8-10, 16; Numbers 16-17, 20; Hebrews 5:1-4; 7']],
st:[['Appointed to speak for Moses','Exodus 4:14-16'],['Stands with Moses before Pharaoh; his staff becomes a snake','Exodus 7:8-12'],['Holds up Moses\' hands with Hur in the battle against Amalek','Exodus 17:10-12'],['Consecrated as priest with his sons; the priestly garments','Exodus 28-29; Leviticus 8'],['Leads the people in making the golden calf','Exodus 32:1-6'],['First offerings; Aaron blesses the people','Leviticus 9:22-24'],['Sons Nadab and Abihu die for strange fire','Leviticus 10:1-3'],['Day of Atonement instructions','Leviticus 16'],['Challenged by Korah; the staff that budded confirms his priesthood','Numbers 16-17'],['Not allowed into the land at Meribah','Numbers 20:12'],['Dies on Mount Hor; Eleazar takes his place','Numbers 20:22-29']],
pl:['Loyal helper to Moses','Faithful servant at the altar','Silent submission when his sons died (Leviticus 10:3)','Standing between the living and the dead to stop a plague (Numbers 16:47-48)'],
wk:['Caved to the people\'s demand for a calf','Joined Miriam in criticising Moses (Numbers 12)','Blamed the people (Exodus 32:22-24)'],
al:'Aaron was the first priest to officiate at the bronze altar (Leviticus 9) and the altar of incense. His sons Nadab and Abihu died offering unauthorised fire (Leviticus 10:1-2).',
jx:'The book of Hebrews compares Aaron\'s priesthood with Jesus\' (Hebrews 5:1-10; 7:11-28). Aaron\'s sacrifices were repeated; Jesus\' was once for all. Aaron died outside the land; Jesus lives forever to intercede.',
ls:['Leaders must hold the line when the crowd presses.','A priest needs mercy for others because he too is weak (Hebrews 5:2-3).','We need a perfect High Priest, and we have one.','God\'s holiness is not to be treated casually.'],
rd:[['Call and consecration','Exodus 28-29'],['The calf','Exodus 32'],['Strange fire','Leviticus 10'],['Better priesthood','Hebrews 7']],
