st:[['Leads Israel against Amalek','Exodus 17:8-13'],['Stays in the tent of meeting as Moses\' aide','Exodus 33:11'],['One of the twelve spies; with Caleb urges, "Let us go up"','Numbers 13:8, 16; 14:6-9'],['Commissioned to succeed Moses','Numbers 27:15-23; Deuteronomy 31:7-8'],['"Be strong and courageous"; meditate on the Book of the Law','Joshua 1:1-9'],['Sends spies to Jericho; Rahab protects them','Joshua 2'],['Crosses the Jordan on dry ground; twelve stones set up','Joshua 3-4'],['Circumcision and Passover at Gilgal','Joshua 5:1-12'],['Meets the commander of the Lord\'s army','Joshua 5:13-15'],['Jericho\'s walls fall','Joshua 6'],['Defeat at Ai because of Achan\'s sin; victory afterwards','Joshua 7-8'],['Renews the covenant at Ebal and Gerizim','Joshua 8:30-35'],['Deceived by the Gibeonites','Joshua 9'],['The sun stands still at Gibeon','Joshua 10:12-14'],['Divides the land','Joshua 13-21'],['"As for me and my house, we will serve the Lord"','Joshua 24:14-15']],
pl:['Courage and obedience','Dependence on God\'s word','Loyalty to Moses for decades','Led the people in covenant renewal'],
wk:['Did not ask counsel from the Lord about the Gibeonites (Joshua 9:14)','Over-confident at Ai after Jericho'],
al:'After the defeat of Ai, Joshua built an altar of uncut stones on Mount Ebal and offered burnt and peace offerings, writing a copy of the law on the stones (Joshua 8:30-35; Deuteronomy 27:4-8).',
jx:'His name is "Jesus" in Greek. Joshua leads God\'s people into rest in the land; Jesus leads us into the greater rest (Hebrews 4:8-11). The commander of the Lord\'s army (Joshua 5:13-15) is often taken as a pre-incarnate appearance of Christ.',
ls:['Obey God\'s word first, and success follows (Joshua 1:8).','Hidden sin hurts the whole community.','Consult God before major decisions.','Make a clear choice to serve the Lord.'],
rd:[['Commissioning','Joshua 1'],['Crossing the Jordan','Joshua 3-4'],['Jericho and Ai','Joshua 6-8'],['Farewell','Joshua 23-24']],
