st:[['Birth announced by the angel; a Nazirite from birth','Judges 13'],['Marries a Philistine woman at Timnah','Judges 14:1-4'],['Kills a lion; the riddle; the wedding fails','Judges 14'],['Burns the Philistine fields with foxes and torches','Judges 15:1-8'],['Kills a thousand men with a jawbone; God provides water','Judges 15:9-19'],['Carries off the gates of Gaza','Judges 16:1-3'],['Loves Delilah; tells her the secret three times falsely','Judges 16:4-15'],['The hair is cut; "the Lord had left him"','Judges 16:16-20'],['Blinded, bound and made to grind in prison','Judges 16:21'],['Prays at the temple of Dagon; pulls down the pillars','Judges 16:23-30'],['Buried in his father\'s tomb','Judges 16:31']],
pl:['The Spirit of the Lord came upon him mightily (Judges 14:6; 15:14)','Began to deliver Israel (Judges 13:5)','Repentance and prayer at the end'],
wk:['Pursued the desires of his eyes','Played with temptation until he was caught','Careless with his Nazirite vow','Revenge-driven rather than God-driven'],
jx:'Samson\'s death delivered Israel; he "killed more at his death than during his life" (Judges 16:30). Jesus won His greatest victory by dying. Samson is the failing deliverer who points to the perfect Deliverer.',
ls:['Gifts without character are fragile.','Compromise takes us a little at a time.','It is never too late to pray for restoration, but sin has consequences.','God can use even a flawed life (Hebrews 11:32).'],
