st:[['Called before he was born: "I have appointed you a prophet to the nations"','Jeremiah 1:4-10'],['Objects: "I am only a youth"','Jeremiah 1:6-8'],['Temple sermon: "Do not trust in deceptive words"','Jeremiah 7:1-15'],['The potter and the clay','Jeremiah 18:1-12'],['The broken flask; beaten and put in stocks by Pashhur','Jeremiah 19-20'],['Rebuked false prophets who say "peace" when there is no peace','Jeremiah 6:14; 23; 28'],['Letter to the exiles: "seek the welfare of the city"; hope and a future','Jeremiah 29:1-14'],['The new covenant','Jeremiah 31:31-34'],['Buys a field while Jerusalem is under siege','Jeremiah 32'],['The scroll burned by King Jehoiakim; rewritten','Jeremiah 36'],['Thrown into a cistern; rescued by Ebed-melech','Jeremiah 38'],['Jerusalem falls in 586 BC','Jeremiah 39; 52'],['Taken to Egypt against his advice','Jeremiah 42-43'],['Laments over the city','Lamentations 1-5']],
pl:['Faithful in a thankless ministry','Honest with God in prayer and complaint','Courage under persecution','Hope in the midst of judgement'],
wk:['Despair: "Cursed be the day I was born!" (Jeremiah 20:14)','Self-doubt and fear of rejection'],
al:'Jeremiah warned that the Temple and its sacrifices would not save a people who oppressed the poor and worshipped idols (Jeremiah 7:1-11, 21-23).',
jx:'The new covenant of Jeremiah 31:31-34 is sealed in Jesus\' blood (Luke 22:20; Hebrews 8:8-12). Like Jeremiah, Jesus wept over Jerusalem (Luke 19:41) and was rejected by His own people.',
ls:['Obedience is not measured by results.','Be honest with God about your pain.','God has plans for your welfare even in exile (Jeremiah 29:11).','The new covenant writes God\'s law on the heart.'],
